Scene summary: Hook: the data officer receives the annual PKP report back from review, covered in yellow sticky notes asking for revisions; the format and the data per cluster were not consistent. The product does not appear. 9:16 vertical, realistic live-action, shot on a modern smartphone | Primary Video Type: UGC Native (Pengelola data puskesmas menerima laporan PKP yang dikembalikan untuk direvisi) + Supporting Format: Product Demo | Handheld medium shots in a small puskesmas staff room in the late afternoon; one close-up of a report folder covered with yellow sticky notes; Seq 3 single static tripod medium shot at the same desk. REFERENCE PRIORITY: Use DNA Character as the authority for the talent's FACE and BODY identity only (not the outfit). Use DNA Product as the authority for the exact product identity. WARDROBE below overrides any outfit visible in the DNA Character image. CHARACTER LOCK: Use the DNA Character reference ONLY for the talent's face and body identity: exact face shape, jawline, skin tone, eye shape, eyebrows, hair or hijab style, body proportions and distinguishing features. Do NOT copy the outfit from the reference image; the outfit is defined in WARDROBE below. Keep the exact same face and body throughout the sequence. Do not add accessories or name tags not listed in WARDROBE. WARDROBE (OVERRIDES REFERENCE OUTFIT): Dusty pink instant hijab, navy long-sleeve blouse with small white dots, black long skirt, black flat shoes, clear-framed glasses, simple rose-gold watch. No name tag, no lanyard, no badge. PRODUCT LOCK: Exact Kit PKP Puskesmas 2026 per Klaster ILP package from the DNA Product reference image (the real package mockup uploaded as an ingredient). Preserve the exact box colors, title text, cover design, proportions and visible design details exactly as in the reference. Do NOT invent a different box design. It may appear with a printed annual PKP report example in a clear folder, a printed management checklist, and a laptop showing the package's Excel tools (a colorful indicator recap with two charts, and a sheet listing the lowest indicators highlighted in red). Do not redesign, simplify, recolor, or rebrand the box. SET & PROPS: Small puskesmas staff room in the late afternoon: a simple desk with a laptop, a thick report folder covered in yellow sticky notes (no readable text), a water dispenser, gray lockers, a wall clock, warm low sun through the window blinds, no other people. TIMELINE — 10 seconds: 0–2s Hook · close-up: a thick report folder with many yellow sticky notes is set down on the desk (no readable text); cut to medium shot as she looks up to the camera. VO (ID, verbatim): "Laporan PKP kami dikembalikan." Delivery (EN): disappointed, low voice 2–4s Problem · medium shot, she peels one sticky note and reads it. VO (ID, verbatim): "Diminta revisi di banyak bagian." Delivery (EN): honest 4–6s Problem · medium close-up, she flips between two pages with different table layouts. VO (ID, verbatim): "Format tiap klaster beda-beda." Delivery (EN): frustrated but calm 6–8s Problem · medium shot, she glances at the wall clock, then back to camera. VO (ID, verbatim): "Harus diperbaiki cepat." Delivery (EN): worried 8–10s Beat · medium shot, she takes off her glasses and rubs the bridge of her nose. VO: none. AUDIO: Quiet late-afternoon room tone, water dispenser bubbling, paper rustling. Only the talent speaks. Natural Indonesian, conversational, clear pronunciation, no background music. Lighting/mood: realistic natural light matching the set, clean soft contrast, believable Indonesian setting, not glossy, not studio. Camera: follow the camera style above consistently; stable and restrained, no whip pans, no drone, no 360 orbit. Keep product readable whenever it is on screen. Performance: natural facial expression, believable professional UGC, natural eye contact, restrained gestures, no exaggerated acting. Lips clearly synced to each word. Hands: simple, natural, relaxed movements. CLEAN OUTPUT: No subtitles, captions, generated text overlays, watermark, poster layout, storyboard panels, or added graphics. Do not invent product details, claims, prices, ratings, testimonials, certifications, or guarantees. Keep exact talent face, the WARDROBE above, product shape, colors, packaging, box, printed report, laptop screen, laptop screen content, and visual details consistent with the DNA references.